Disclosed update check: when the user presses "install update", the official
desktop cashier adds an X-Delivery-Token header (a licence fingerprint, a scope
and an expiry, signed; not the licence key; no user activity or personal data)
to its request for the update manifest at the-live.shop. It can only make the
author's update server refuse an update, never disable a copy that is running.

